STAFF COMMENTS:  

This bill meets the criteria to be placed on the Suspense  
file.

Staff notes that while this bill appropriates a total of  
$192.3 million, under the provisions of the bill only funds  
for planning grants can be expended during fiscal year  
1999-2000 (a maximum of $21.5 million for 431 schools)  the  
balance cannot be expended until fiscal year 2000-01.  The  
costs, which will begin to be incurred immediately upon  
enactment of this bill, are to the SPI and SBE, and no  
appropriation is included for them.  Therefore, staff  
recommends this bill be amended either: 1) to delete $172.8  
million of the appropriation and substitute intent language  
that these amounts be appropriated in the 2000 Budget Act  
or 2) to delay the effective date of these appropriations  
until July 1, 2000.  In addition, staff recommends the bill  
be amended to include an appropriation for administrative  
expenses to the SPI and SBE from the effective date of the  
bill through fiscal year 1999-2000. 

The actual costs for the GHAISP and IIUSP depend upon the  
number of participating schools and the number of pupils in  
those schools.   Apparently the number of participating  
schools will be adjusted to ensure that the appropriated  
funds are expended.  

If less than the number of schools designated in each grade  
level category apply ("volunteer") for intervention,  the  
bill contains a provision whereby the SPI, with SBE  
approval, shall randomly select schools from schools  










scoring below the 50th percentile.  This provision creates  
a mandate for those schools, which are selected, rather  
than volunteer, for the program.  Mandated costs could  
include any costs necessary to implement the plan, which  
are in excess of the $150 per pupil grant, including the  
required local match.  The committee may wish to consider  
eliminating the mandate from the bill, and making the  
program entirely voluntary.











































